Package: risikoR
Title: Simulate, Analyse and Play the Board Game Risk
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Raban", "Heller", email = "raban.heller@charite.de",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742"))
Description: A toolkit for the board game Risk (German "Risiko"). Provides the
    dice-combat engine, single-battle and whole-conquest simulators, closed-form
    and Monte Carlo win probabilities, a full game state model with a world map
    and adjacency graph, scriptable artificial-intelligence agents, and a
    'ggplot2' visualisation layer for maps, dice-duel outcomes and probability
    curves. An interactive 'shiny' application supports playing, simulating and
    analysing games. Combat resolution follows the standard rules in which the
    attacker rolls up to three dice and the defender up to two, comparing the
    highest dice pairwise with ties going to the defender.
